## Usage

```elixir
{:ok, result} = AshGraphLaw.Capability.API.{{ op_name }}([{% for f in request_fields | filter(attribute="op_name", value=op_name) | filter(attribute="field_required", value="true") %}{{ f.field_name }}: {% if f.field_type == "integer" %}1{% elif f.field_type == "boolean" %}true{% elif f.field_type == "object" or f.field_type == "term" %}%{}{% elif f.field_type is starting_with("list<") %}[]{% else %}"..."{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}])
```

`run/2` accepts the options of `AshGraphLaw.call/2` (server, timeouts, fuel). The request is
built and validated client-side without the engine; the call itself runs on the real engine.

